  <descriptions><description xml:lang="eng" descriptionType="Abstract">We report the polarization measurement of a very high order (59th and 61st order, similar to 17 nm) harmonic. A Mo-Si multilayer mirror is used as a polarizer with reflectivity of 60% and polarization analyzing power close 'to unity around a wavelength of 17 nm. We observe that for these high harmonics in Ne there is no rotation of the polarization ellipse with respect to the fundamental laser polarization, even though the harmonics are in the plateau. For linear and slightly elliptical laser polarization the harmonics still remain linearly polarized. These findings are supported by a full theoretical simulation, which includes spatiotemporal integration and phase matching of the emitted harmonic radiation.</description>  </descriptions>
